Description
Hi team, one weird issue that I found when I tried to forget permits from a closed semaphore: it's reopened again.
I think there're a few acceptable behaviors:

Reject the forget operation by returning status
Decrement the permit count, but it should be kept closed

I tried this code:
#[test]
fn forget_permits_on_closed_semaphore_must_stay_closed() {
    let s = Semaphore::new(10);
    s.close();

    assert!(s.is_closed());
    assert_eq!(s.available_permits(), 10);
    assert_eq!(s.forget_permits(4), 4);

    // BUG: after forget_permits, the semaphore should still be closed,
    // but forget_permits clears the CLOSED bit from the atomic permits counter.
    assert!(
        s.is_closed(),
        "semaphore should still be closed after forget_permits"
    );
    assert_eq!(s.available_permits(), 6);
}

