Description
As described in #tokio-internals, tokio::mpsc::Chan::recv_many makes incorrect assumptions about the provided buffer when exiting through the post-loop rx_fields.rx_closed && self.inner.semaphore.is_idle() code path.
assert!(buffer.is_empty()); asserts the incorrect precondition, it should assert_eq!(buffer.len(), initial_length); instead.
The following tests trigger the faulty assertion for bounded and unbounded channels:
